{
  "duration": 86.259,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.419,
      "text": "So welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.819,
      "end": 3.159,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.679,
      "end": 5.159,
      "text": "Now in this problem, we are given that"
    },
    {
      "start": 5.599,
      "end": 8.159,
      "text": "two cyclists are moving in the same direction."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.619,
      "end": 11.579,
      "text": "The speed of the slower cyclist is eighteen kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.159,
      "end": 13.019,
      "text": "After three hours,"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.42,
      "end": 16.279,
      "text": "the faster cyclist is twenty-seven kilometer ahead."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.859,
      "end": 20.26,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find the speed of the faster cyclist."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.68,
      "end": 23.899,
      "text": "Now let the speed of the faster cyclist be x kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.519,
      "end": 24.819,
      "text": "First,"
    },
    {
      "start": 25.18,
      "end": 28.42,
      "text": "let us find how much distance each cyclist covers in three hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.939,
      "end": 29.84,
      "text": "We know the formula,"
    },
    {
      "start": 30.42,
      "end": 32.52,
      "text": "distance is equal to speed into time."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.18,
      "end": 36.119,
      "text": "The slower cyclist covers eighteen into three,"
    },
    {
      "start": 36.579,
      "end": 39.34,
      "text": "which is fifty-four kilometers in three hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.84,
      "end": 41.659,
      "text": "The faster cyclist covers"
    },
    {
      "start": 42.04,
      "end": 46.639,
      "text": "x into three, which is three x kilometers in three hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 47.119,
      "end": 49.039,
      "text": "Now let us understand the given condition."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.639,
      "end": 50.699,
      "text": "After three hours,"
    },
    {
      "start": 51.079,
      "end": 61.239,
      "text": "the faster cyclist is twenty-seven kilometer ahead. This simply means that the faster cyclist has covered twenty-seven kilometer more than the slower cyclist."
    },
    {
      "start": 61.639,
      "end": 69.059,
      "text": "So distance covered by the faster cyclist minus distance covered by the slower cyclist is equal to twenty-seven."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.519,
      "end": 81.879,
      "text": "That gives us three x minus fifty-four is equal to twenty-seven. After solving this, x is equal to twenty-seven kilometer per hour, so the speed of the faster cyclist is twenty-seven"
    },
    {
      "start": 82.58,
      "end": 86.259,
      "text": "kilometer per hour. Hence, the correct answer is option C."
    }
  ],
